      "safety_contract": "The engine remains the sole compute owner. The two-slot default gives concurrent streaming requests bounded round-robin token stepping; a lone active stream retains Metal encode-ahead, contended rounds suppress future session-local graphs before yielding to keep the shared Metal queue unblocked, and cancellation plus terminal events are observed at every yield. Exclusive engine work is dequeued in post order rather than behind the streaming batch, the bounded engine channel is never drained into an unbounded local queue so QueueFull->503 stays reachable during streaming, each job owns the engine slot for its whole life so the stall watchdog still observes it, and runs driven by the process-global CUDA resident engine stay run-to-completion. CAMELID_CONTINUOUS_BATCH_SLOTS=1 restores run-to-completion scheduling everywhere."
